diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index deca8f1..bb77a4f 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -390,6 +390,14 @@ at a time, forever. Labels may overlap across pools.
 | `runner_group` | no | `Default` | Org-scoped pools only — see below |
 | `liveness_timeout` | no | `5m` | How long a freshly booted runner may take to show up online before the slot is torn down and recycled |
 | `drain_timeout` | no | `30m` | On shutdown, how long a busy runner may finish its job before being powered down (the job then fails — GitHub does not requeue jobs from vanished ephemeral runners). systemd `TimeoutStopSec` (35m in the shipped unit) must exceed the largest pool value |
+| `job_timeout` | no | `6h` | Host execution limit starting when GitHub first reports the runner busy; idle waiting does not count. Set above the longest workflow job timeout, including cancellation grace. |
+
+After registration the controller keeps checking runner status. A deleted runner
+is reclaimed even if its guest refuses shutdown. A runner continuously reported
+offline for `liveness_timeout` is also reclaimed; API errors interrupt that
+offline grace period. Once observed busy, the `job_timeout` deadline persists
+through status changes and API errors. Controller shutdown still uses the
+existing drain policy. Guest cooperation is not required for reclamation.
 
 Oversubscription (`sum(count × cpus/memory)` beyond the host) is allowed
 but warned about by `setup` and at controller startup.
